WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.828
Retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG, uses external or indexed material as context for model responses.

00:00:06.828 --> 00:00:14.371
Instead of placing every document into the prompt, the system retrieves chunks that appear relevant to the question.

00:00:14.371 --> 00:00:20.159
Chunk size, overlap, metadata, source labels, and ranking all affect what the model sees.

00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:25.946
Retrieval can be efficient, but it can also hide important missing or irrelevant context.

00:00:25.946 --> 00:00:34.855
Long-context workflows offer an alternative: include larger source sets directly, or include retrieved material plus surrounding context.

00:00:34.855 --> 00:00:42.983
This can help the model compare sources, resolve contradictions, or inspect evidence that a narrow retrieval step might miss.

00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:45.454
Hybrid approaches are often strongest.

00:00:45.454 --> 00:00:52.737
Retrieval narrows the field, and large context lets the model review the selected material with more continuity.

00:00:52.737 --> 00:00:54.337
Provenance is essential.

00:00:54.337 --> 00:01:02.596
Retrieved chunks should carry source names, locations, timestamps, version information, or other metadata that supports review.

00:01:02.596 --> 00:01:09.164
When the model makes a claim, users should be able to trace it back to the material that informed it.

00:01:09.164 --> 00:01:12.350
Citations and source tracking are not decorative.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.796
They are how long-context workflows remain auditable.

00:01:15.796 --> 00:01:18.333
Avoid blind trust in retrieval results.

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:23.015
Retrieved material can be irrelevant, stale, incomplete, or adversarial.

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:27.957
Prompt injection in retrieved content can try to override the intended task.

00:01:27.957 --> 00:01:33.744
The model should treat retrieved content as data to analyze, not as instructions to obey.

00:01:33.744 --> 00:01:40.273
Long context gives room for evidence, but the workflow still needs source review and human judgement.
